  "answer_text": "**ProFed Credit Union** (legally *ProFed Federal Credit Union*) is a member-owned, not-for-profit financial cooperative headquartered in Fort Wayne, Indiana. Founded in 1933, the credit union serves individuals, families, and businesses across Northeast Indiana.\n\nIts official web portal is **[profedcu.org](https://www.profedcu.org)** (which is also reachable via **profedcreditunion.com**). \n\n---\n\n### **Who is Eligible to Join?**\nProFed operates as a community charter credit union. You are eligible to become a member if you live, work, worship, attend school, volunteer, or regularly conduct business in any of the following **nine Northeast Indiana counties**:\n* Adams, Allen, DeKalb, Huntington, LaGrange, Noble, Steuben, Wells, and Whitley.\n\nImmediate family members of existing ProFed members are also eligible to join. A minimum deposit of **$5** into a savings account is required to establish your membership and ownership share.\n\n---\n\n### **Services & Products Offered**\nProFed functions similarly to a traditional bank, but profits are returned to members in the form of lower fees, higher savings yields, and competitive loan rates. Their main offerings include:\n\n* **Personal Banking:** Savings and checking accounts, debit cards, and certificates of deposit (CDs).\n* **Loans:** Auto loans, recreational vehicle (RV) loans, home mortgages, personal loans, and home equity lines of credit (HELOCs).\n* **Credit Cards:** Options like the ProFed Visa\u00ae Rewards card.\n* **Business Services:** Business checking, commercial lending, and cash management.\n* **Financial Advisors:** Personalized investment, retirement planning, and wealth management advice through ProFed Financial Advisors.\n* **Digital Banking:** A robust online platform and mobile app (available on iOS and Android) that supports mobile deposits, bill pay, person-to-person payments, and inclusive accessibility features.\n\n---\n\n### **Branch Locations & Access**\nProFed operates **13 branch locations** throughout Northeast Indiana, including multiple offices in Fort Wayne, Decatur, Angola, and Kendallville. \n* **Corporate Office / Main Branch:** 1710 St. Joe River Dr., Fort Wayne, IN 46805.\n* **ATM Network:** Members have surcharge-free access to a large nationwide network of ATMs.\n* **Video Tellers:** In addition to standard lobby hours, many locations feature drive-up Video Tellers with extended hours. \n\nIf you want to open an account, apply for a loan, or log in to your digital banking, you can visit their official website at **[profedcu.org](https://www.profedcu.org)**.",
